        <title><![CDATA[Bitcoin and Blockchain Basics]]></title>
        <link>https://www.theblock.co/learn/bitcoin/bitcoin-and-blockchain-basics-434447</link>
        <media:content url="https://www.tbstat.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=1600,height=900,fit=cover,format=jpeg,quality=80/wp/uploads/2026/11/bitcoin201.png" type="image/*" medium="image"/>        <guid isPermaLink="false">4de08de3-4a9f-5657-b84e-e1cf7bc8c2bd</guid>
        <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:43:50 +0000</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[Bitcoin is presented as the first cryptocurrency. It is a decentralized digital currency with a fixed supply of 21 million coins, a peer-to-peer network, Proof of Work security, and transparent but pseudonymous transactions.
The important beginner idea is not only that Bitcoin is digital money. It is that Bitcoin showed how a network could record value transfers without relying on a single company, government, or bank to update the ledger.]]></description>            <dc:creator><![CDATA[The Block Research]]></dc:creator>
